[gd_scene load_steps=30 format=3]

; Tri-axle flatbed semi-trailer. Hand-built low-poly (Kenney ships no trailers at all), flat
; boxes and 10-segment cylinders to match the kit's flat-shaded look.
;
; AUTHORED WITH THE ORIGIN AT THE KINGPIN, ground at y = -1.05 — measured off the tractor unit's
; fifth-wheel plate, whose top face is 1.05 m above the road. That makes the coupling datum the
; origin, so Articulation.coupled_pose is one transform multiply and the joint sits exactly on
; this node. It is the implements' convention in the same shape ("origin on the lower pin line,
; ground at y = -0.21"), and for the same reason: the geometry lives here and is MEASURED off it,
; never restated as constants in code.
;
; Sizes are measured against the shipped kit, not against real trucks: the sedan is 1.80 m wide
; and 2.88 long, the garbage truck 1.92 x 3.85 x 1.72. So this is 1.92 wide (truck-family width)
; with a 5.40 m deck behind a 1.35 m neck, and the whole rig behind the 3.40 m tractor unit comes
; to ~8.9 m.
;
; IT IS A GOOSENECK, AND THAT IS STRUCTURAL RATHER THAN DECORATIVE. NOTHING of the trailer may hang
; below the coupling plane (y = 0) over the tractor: the front 1.35 m is a raised NECK whose
; underside is the bolster plate, and the frame + deck step DOWN behind the tractor's tail (from
; z 1.05, which clears its rear bumper at z 0.96 in this frame). Authored flat instead — one deck
; height end to end, 0.46 m BELOW the plate — the deck and both frame rails ran straight through
; the tractor's own frame rails, mudguards and fifth wheel. A real semi-trailer has this shape for
; exactly this reason.
;
; The clearances that are geometry rather than taste:
;   - the front overhang is 0.33 m (the neck, which is the frontmost part), so the front corners
;     swing on sqrt(0.96^2 + 0.33^2) = 1.02 m, INSIDE the 1.15 m from the kingpin to the cab's rear
;     face. A real artic is built to exactly this rule, and it is what lets the rig fold right round
;     without the trailer reaching the cab. test_trailer measures it off this scene.
;   - the landing legs are authored RETRACTED, feet 0.14 m clear of the road, because the trailer
;     spawns coupled. There is nothing to lower them with and they are not collision.
;
; Undriven and unsteered: the axles only ever brake. Suspension/mass/grip live in
; flatbed_spec.tres, wheels are the kit's own truck wheel scaled on the INSTANCE (RayWheel
; overwrites each Wheels/* root transform every tick, so the scale must ride the child).

