; The bolster plate: the trailer's own steel face, which RESTS ON TOP of the tractor's fifth wheel.
; It sits ABOVE the origin plane (y = 0.02 .. 0.10) and the tractor's plate ends AT it (world
; 0.95 .. 1.05), so the two are stacked with a 2 cm gap rather than sharing the same slab of space —
; authored coplanar they z-fought into one flickering white slab, which is what this comment exists
; to stop happening again. It is deliberately NARROWER than the fifth wheel (1.14) so the plate the
; tractor unit is recognised by stays visible from the side.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="MeshPlate"]
material = SubResource("MatSteel")
size = Vector3(1.06, 0.08, 1.0)

; The pin, hanging below the bolster plate into the fifth wheel's jaws: mostly swallowed by the
; tractor's plate, with the 2 cm of it that crosses the gap visible.
[sub_resource type="CylinderMesh" id="MeshKingpin"]
material = SubResource("MatSteel")
top_radius = 0.065
bottom_radius = 0.065
height = 0.18
radial_segments = 10
rings = 1

; The neck: it sits ON the bolster plate (0.10) and its top is the trailer's front deck level, so
; nothing here reaches below the coupling plane.
[sub_resource type="BoxMesh" id="MeshNeck"]
material = SubResource("MatFrame")
size = Vector3(1.92, 0.16, 1.38)

; The step face closing the drop from the neck down to the deck.
